    shortDesc: "Custom foam inserts cut to your product and your box \u2014 EVA, sponge, pearl cotton or card fitments, with flocked surfaces. From 200 sets with your box order.",
    intro: "The insert is what holds your product still in transit, presents it at the right angle when the lid opens, and lets the customer lift it out cleanly without tugging. ELAPACK die-cuts custom inserts for the custom packaging boxes we manufacture \u2014 across jewelry, fragrance, skincare and gift sets \u2014 specified together with the outer box from day one, so the cavity, the box interior and the product are engineered as a single fitment rather than separate orders hoped into alignment. This page covers custom inserts supplied for presentation and retail packaging boxes.",
    description: "EVA foam \u2014 dense, firm and clean-edged; holds intricate multi-cavity layouts and heavier items such as glass perfume bottles and cosmetic jars without deforming. Sponge \u2014 soft, high-recovery cushioning suited to lightweight or delicate pieces where gentle compression matters. Pearl cotton (EPE) \u2014 lightweight, closed-cell shock absorption where the insert serves primarily as a transit-protection layer. Paper-card fitments \u2014 the printable alternative or companion: standalone folded card platforms and dividers, or printed card fitments paired with a foam base so care notes and branding sit beside the product.\n\nFoam surfaces can be finished with custom flocking \u2014 the soft, velvety surface standard in fine jewelry and watch boxes \u2014 in shades matched to your brand palette. Foam density and wall thickness are never picked blind from a chart: they follow your product's weight, fragility and centre of gravity, and are proven on a loaded sample. If you are still weighing foam against other insert systems, our packaging inserts guide covers the full material comparison; this page is where your chosen box insert gets specified and ordered.\n\nSend us your product drawing, dieline or a physical unit alongside the box format you have in mind. We engineer the cavity layout \u2014 recess depth, perimeter wall allowance, and finger notches for effortless lifting \u2014 and cut a physical prototype. We test the sample loaded with your actual product inside to check retention, presentation height and surface clearance. Mass production follows that approved loaded sample, not an untested drawing.\n\nBecause your insert is engineered alongside the box, the flocking shade is matched to the inner lid lining, any companion card fitment is printed on the same press run as the outer wrap, and the complete assembly ships together \u2014 so the insert ships fitted with its box, not as a separate follow-up.\n\nHow ordering works: send your product dimensions (or mail a physical unit), weight and fragility notes, and the target box style. We recommend the insert material and cavity layout, and quote the insert together with your box within 1 business day. Approve the loaded physical sample tested with your product in place. Bulk production runs after sample sign-off and payment; inserts ship pre-fitted inside their boxes or packed together as matched sets.",
