    "body": "*This is a buyer specification guide. Fit, fibre contact and performance depend on the actual wig, construction and sample; confirm them for your order.*\n\nWig brands and salon buyers often need a storage bag, a presentation box or both. Start with the wig in the form it will be packed, then decide how the customer will receive and store it. A bag, box and shipping outer have different jobs; the choice depends on your product and route. This guide helps you prepare a comparable supplier brief. For a selected bag option, see [custom satin wig bags](https://elapack.com/products/custom-satin-wig-bag/); for the broader combination, see [custom wig packaging](https://elapack.com/custom-wig-packaging/).\n\n## Key takeaways\n\n- Measure the actual folded or supported wig, including cap, net, tags and accessories; do not assign one bag size to every style.\n- Check contact surfaces, seams and drawstring movement with the actual hair on a loaded sample. A fabric name alone cannot establish protection.\n- Quote each component of a bag-and-box set separately. ELAPACK's stated minimum is 200 pieces per component; confirm sizes, versions and prices in writing.\n\n![Wig packaging buyer checklist: measure the packed wig, compare bag or box, review a loaded sample](/charts/wig-packaging-buyer-checklist.svg)\n\n## Which packaging format fits the selling route?\n\nChoose the route before the structure. A fabric bag can be the storage piece after purchase. A presentation box can carry retail artwork and provide a defined opening. An outer carton addresses distribution handling. If you want a bag inside a box, ask for a loaded sample of the combined assembly. Do not assume that either format alone prevents tangling, compression or transport damage.\n\nFor boxed hair extensions sold by length or shade, use the [hair extension boxes product page](https://elapack.com/products/custom-hair-extension-boxes/) to specify item count, insert contact, label visibility and version quantities. It serves a different buyer task from a full-wig storage bag.\n\n## How should the wig be measured for a bag or box?\n\nRecord the packed length, width and depth of each wig style, including its cap, support, protective net and any card. Say whether it is folded, laid flat or supported. For a bag, state the usable interior space needed after the drawstring is closed; for a box, state the loaded arrangement and how the wig will be removed. A 30 \xD7 40 cm option appears in the current satin-bag product record, but it is not a fit standard for all wigs. Decide size from the actual item and approve a sample.\n\nCheck the longest and fullest styles in the planned range, not just the smallest sample. Record quantities by size, color and artwork version so the supplier can confirm what the stated minimum covers. For a bag-and-box set, request the minimum and quotation for each component.\n\n## What should a loaded sample prove?\n\nPut your own wig into the proposed bag or box and inspect the fabric contact, seams, closure, insert and removal sequence. Open and close the bag repeatedly; look at contact near the drawstring and stitching. For a box, check usable space and any insert against the actual cap and hair. Note what you observe rather than assuming a material or structure guarantees a condition after shipping. If transit performance matters, agree on the packing method and test scope for that order.\n\nReview branding on the proposed material. Supply the logo file, placement, color reference and proposed method, then approve a physical or agreed digital proof for the relevant surface. Satin sheen and artwork position can change how a mark appears; the sample is the place to settle that decision.\n\n## What belongs in the first quote request?\n\nCopy this brief into your own purchasing record:\n\n1. Wig styles, quantities and the packed dimensions for each style.\n2. Requested bag, box, shipping outer or matched set; each component's quantity.\n3. Proposed contact material, seams, closure or insert; any handling issue to check on a loaded sample.\n4. Artwork files, colors, label information and version allocation.\n5. Sample type, destination and target date; ask the supplier to confirm feasibility, price and production timing in writing.\n\nELAPACK lists a 200-piece minimum; a matched set has a 200-piece minimum for each component. Production is typically 15\u201320 days after sample approval and payment receipt, with shipping separate; confirm the actual order schedule. The current [satin wig bag](https://elapack.com/products/custom-satin-wig-bag/) and [custom wig packaging](https://elapack.com/custom-wig-packaging/) pages provide the product and combination routes. Use the [contact form](https://elapack.com/contact/) when you are ready to request a specific quotation. This guide itself does not establish fit or a performance guarantee.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [ELAPACK custom satin wig bag](https://elapack.com/products/custom-satin-wig-bag/) \u2014 product option and stated MOQ; fit is confirmed on an order-specific sample.\n- [ELAPACK custom wig packaging](https://elapack.com/custom-wig-packaging/) \u2014 bag, box and set route; specifications require an actual-item review.\n- [ELAPACK custom hair extension boxes](https://elapack.com/products/custom-hair-extension-boxes/) \u2014 separate bundle-box specification task and inquiry route.\n",
