    "readTime": "4 min read",
    "image": "/images/covers/custom-glasses-cases-pouches-guide-reviewed.png",
    "imageAlt": "Illustrative buyer checklist: choose the eyewear protection task \u2014 not a product photograph.",
    "imageWidth": 2400,
    "imageHeight": 1350,
    "excerpt": "Compare eyewear pouch and packaging-box proposals by frame fit, material contact, closure and branding. Confirm hard-case supply separately.",
    "metaDescription": "Compare soft glasses pouches and packaging boxes by frame dimensions, closure and branding. Confirm hard-case supply separately before quoting.",
    "body": "*Ordering terms are as published on our [eyewear packaging](https://elapack.com/eyewear-packaging/) page.*\n\nThis guide focuses on pouch and presentation-box selection for eyewear. Confirm current product availability and any protective or cleaning requirement in the project quotation. Hard cases require a separate construction review.\n\n> **Quick answer:** compare the actual folded frames, intended use and required protection with the proposed pouch, case or box. Confirm the selected construction and supply scope; neither a soft pouch nor a presentation box establishes crush protection. ELAPACK MOQ is 200 pieces, with typical production 15\u201320 days after sample approval and payment, subject to the order.\n\n## Key takeaways\n\n- Start from the folded frames: their dimensions set the footprint for the pouch, the case and the box \u2014 share them in the enquiry.\n- A pouch, a hard case and a presentation box do different jobs; neither a soft pouch nor a presentation box establishes crush protection.\n- Do not assume a pouch doubles as a lens cloth \u2014 cleaning needs its own material-specific advice and an agreed test.\n- Confirm the actual construction and supply scope before sampling; format names alone establish nothing.\n- Ordering terms in one place: MOQ 200 pieces (each component of a set 200), custom sample USD 30 + USD 25 shipping in 3\u20135 days, production typically 15\u201320 days after sample approval and payment.\n\n## Custom words and personalised words\n\nCustomisation can concern dimensions, artwork, material or presentation. State which changes are needed and whether the task is retail presentation, daily storage, carrying or cleaning. Keyword wording alone does not establish two distinct buyer groups or prove demand for a particular material.\n\n![Illustrative buyer checklist: choose the eyewear protection task](/charts/glasses-case-formats-reviewed-20261022.svg)\n\n**State the intended use and the proposed construction in the enquiry.**\n\n## Formats: the honest map\n\n| Candidate format | Construction to confirm | Buyer review |\n|---|---|---|\n| Hard or semi-hard case | Actual shell, covering, hinge and closure | Supply feasibility, frame fit and required protection |\n| Soft pouch | Actual fabric, seams and closure | Loaded fit, contact and intended storage |\n| Presentation box | Actual board construction and fitted support | Frame removal, retention and any shipping outer |\n| Collapsible concept | Actual folds, assembly and packed dimensions | Availability, assembly and loaded fit |\n\nConfirm the actual supply scope before sampling. A pouch, rigid case and presentation box perform different tasks; none should be substituted for another without reviewing the required fit and protection.\n\n## How do you decide on the pouch?\n\nCompare the actual fabric, seam placement, usable opening and closure against the folded frame. Material names do not establish cleaning performance or compatibility with lens coatings. If cleaning is required, obtain material-specific care advice and an agreed test; do not assume any pouch doubles as a lens cloth. Use the [sunglasses pouch guide](https://elapack.com/news/custom-sunglasses-pouches-guide/) and [logo guide](https://elapack.com/news/custom-logo-pouches-guide/) to prepare sample questions. Confirm branding feasibility on the proposed fabric rather than applying a universal colour-count rule.\n\n## Why do the frames set the box footprint?\n\nA folded pair of glasses defines the box interior \u2014 share the folded frame dimensions and the box and insert get built around them, the same rule our eyewear collection page publishes. Standard decisions:\n\n| Decision | Options | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| Construction | rigid two-piece, magnetic flip-lid, fold-flat | magnetic pairs with the [magnetic gift box guide](https://elapack.com/news/magnetic-gift-boxes-guide/) |\n| Insert | confirm actual material, geometry and contact surface | insert materials compared in [packaging inserts](https://elapack.com/news/packaging-inserts-guide/) |\n| Program | single-frame box, two-frame gift set, box + pouch + card | sets mirror the [jewellery packaging](https://elapack.com/news/custom-jewelry-packaging-guide/) playbook |\n\n## What are the ordering terms?\n\n| Line item | Terms |\n|---|---|\n| MOQ | 200 pieces; confirm design allocation and component scope. Complete sets: each component 200 pieces |\n| Production | typically 15\u201320 days after sample approval and payment receipt; confirm by order |\n| Stock sample | free; USD 25 courier; delivery 4\u20137 days |\n| Custom sample | USD 30 + USD 25 shipping, sample making 3\u20135 days from confirmed artwork; transit and review time are separate |\n| Payment and freight | T/T or PayPal; air or sea from Shanghai or Shenzhen |\n\n## Bottom line\n\nDefine the intended use, folded frame dimensions and protection requirements, then confirm the proposed components and actual supplier responsibilities. Coordinate box and pouch artwork where both are needed, and approve physical samples across the different materials.\n\n**Spec an eyewear packaging program:** send folded frame dimensions and artwork status through the [contact page](https://elapack.com/contact/), or start from the [eyewear packaging collection](https://elapack.com/eyewear-packaging/). For the wider trust checklist before a deposit, see [how to vet a packaging manufacturer](https://elapack.com/news/how-to-vet-a-packaging-manufacturer/). For the soft side of the programme in depth, the [custom sunglasses pouches guide](https://elapack.com/news/custom-sunglasses-pouches-guide/) covers fabric, closure and print on pouches, and the [custom microfiber cloths guide](https://elapack.com/news/custom-microfiber-cloths-guide/) covers the lens cloths that pair with them.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [ELAPACK eyewear packaging](https://elapack.com/eyewear-packaging/) \u2014 the ordering terms this guide follows, as published on the collection page.\n- ELAPACK confirmed trade terms \u2014 the MOQ, sample and production terms stated in the ordering table."
