    "body": "*This guide distinguishes scent-testing paper from a printed carrier for a vial or sachet. Material, fragrance application, printing compatibility and transport eligibility require project-specific confirmation. It does not state that a mounted fragrance sample can be mailed without protective packaging.*\n\n> **Quick answer:** identify what the card carries, how the fragrance is presented and how the pack will be distributed. Specify the actual sample and carrier together; a wallet-size label, GSM figure or flat appearance does not establish scent performance or postal eligibility.\n\n## Key takeaways\n\n- Separate a scent-testing blotter from a printed carrier for a vial or sachet.\n- Specify the actual sample, attachment, artwork and complete packed dimensions together.\n- Confirm material suitability and shipping eligibility for the project; a flat card alone proves neither.\n\n![Perfume sample card formats: scent-testing strip, flat or folded carrier, pocket carrier and vial-on-card concept; confirm the actual sample and scope.](/charts/perfume-sample-cards-formats.svg)\n\n## What functions can a perfume sample card serve?\n\nA blotter is intended to receive fragrance for evaluation. A vial-on-card carrier holds a separate sample. A folded or flat printed card can present instructions and branding without itself functioning as a blotter. Do not assume those constructions use the same paper or that a print substrate is suitable for scent testing.\n\n| Concept to discuss | Input needed | Check before approval |\n|---|---|---|\n| Scent-testing strip | Fragrance and evaluation task | Suitable substrate and fragrance interaction |\n| Flat or folded carrier | Actual sample, count and layout | Retention, access and information |\n| Pocket-format card | Intended finished dimensions and contents | Fit in the proposed envelope or display |\n| Vial-on-card | Vial, closure, fill and attachment proposal | Retention, leakage risk and protective outer |\n\nThese are enquiry concepts, not confirmation that every fragrance application or sample format is supplied. Confirm the exact scope and responsibilities in writing.\n\n## How should material and artwork be reviewed?\n\nAsk for the paper reference, weight, finish and proposed print process. A marketplace GSM range is not an ELAPACK stock specification or proof of absorbency. For scent-sensitive work, review whether paper, coating, adhesive or print affects the intended experience.\n\nA low-odour or low-migration ink description does not alone establish suitability for the fragrance, and evidence developed for another packaging application should not be transferred without review. Agree an appropriate physical sample and acceptance criteria for the actual formulation and carrier.\n\nProvide logo, copy, intended colours and required instructions. Develop the artwork on the agreed drawing, with the sample position, fold, attachment and removal method shown. Free digital dieline previews support structure approval; they do not replace material or fragrance testing.\n\n## How should you size the complete assembly?\n\nMeasure the actual vial, sachet or other sample and specify its orientation and count. Distinguish usable space, finished external dimensions and print bleed. Do not impose a bank-card standard on every pocket carrier or assume that one dieline covers all constructions.\n\nReview whether the recipient can remove and use the sample without tearing required information or damaging the contents. If it is part of a discovery set, coordinate the carrier with the [packaging insert](https://elapack.com/news/packaging-inserts-guide/) and outer box.\n\n## How should distribution and shipping be checked?\n\nState where the pack will travel and who supplies, fills and assembles the fragrance sample. The card alone does not prevent leaks, breakage or exposure. Ask the carrier or appropriately qualified shipping provider to assess the actual contents, quantity, route and required documentation before dispatch.\n\nChoose protective packaging for the complete assembly and agree any required transport checks. Do not infer letter-mail eligibility from a flat-looking card or assume an alcohol-containing sample can use the same service as an empty printed carrier.\n\nFor the related bottle and gift-box task, see the [perfume packaging guide](https://elapack.com/news/custom-perfume-packaging-guide/). A candle-fragrance application needs its own sample and compatibility review rather than automatic reuse of a perfume-card specification.\n\n## What sourcing scope should you compare?\n\nDistinguish unprinted carriers, decorated stock and a newly developed assembly. Compare the same substrate, sample responsibility, attachment, artwork, quantity, packing and destination. Confirm actual availability and current terms; a marketplace listing is not evidence of a supplier's complete custom capability.\n\nELAPACK's MOQ is 200 pieces; confirm the allocation across sizes, colours and artwork in the quotation. Complete sets require 200 pieces of each component. Custom samples are USD 30 plus USD 25 shipping, with a 3\u20135 day sample-making timeframe. Stock samples are free with USD 25 shipping and a stated delivery timeframe of 4\u20137 days. Production is typically 15\u201320 days after sample approval and payment receipt; confirm by order. Free digital dieline previews are provided for structure approval.\n\nFor a printed carrier, review the [custom perfume sample cards product page](https://elapack.com/products/custom-perfume-sample-card-boxes/), then [contact ELAPACK](https://elapack.com/contact/) with the sample type, dimensions, intended distribution and artwork. Confirm the proposed supply scope and verification responsibilities before approving production.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [ELAPACK printed sample card product](https://elapack.com/products/custom-perfume-sample-card-boxes/) \u2014 card-specific brief, conditional materials and attachment.\n- [ELAPACK perfume box product](https://elapack.com/products/custom-perfume-boxes/) \u2014 separate bottle and gift-box brief.\n- [Toffanin sample card product](https://toffanin.it/en/cartoncini-porta-campioncini.html) \u2014 external example of a dedicated sample-card product page; its materials, minimum and capacity are its own."
